  { q: 'What is ghurāb al-bayn in Arabic tradition?', a: 'Ghurāb al-bayn (literally "raven of separation") is the Arabic name for the omen raven of pre-Islamic Arab tradition. The calling of this raven was interpreted as a sign of imminent separation — a loved one leaving, a journey, a parting, or death. This omen raven features extensively in pre-Islamic Arabic poetry (the mu\'allaqāt and other early verse), where the poet hears the ghurāb call and understands that his beloved\'s departure or his own exile is signalled. The ghurāb al-bayn represents the most developed tradition of raven omen interpretation in classical Arabic culture.' },
